consultation_body:
Parties in political consultation: {0}
They accept the ruling party's leadership, keep seats in the legislature and advise on affairs of state:
· A broader base for the government: constitutional legitimacy +{1};
· Discontent has a channel inside the system: public dissent -{2}%;
· They are consulted on the government agenda: parties that agree push it forward, parties that prefer the status quo voice reservations and slow it down, but cannot veto it.
Parties whose ideology is diametrically opposed to the ruling party do not take part and have been dissolved.
